 <h1>HyperDoc Project Workspace</h1>
 <p>HyperDoc's declared project work as one Topic Map. The Work declarations of the <a page="Work Breakdown" hyperbook="dreyeck/work/reading">Work Breakdown</a>, the WBS, plan steps and preconditions of <a page="Authoring the CTM Plan Page" hyperbook="dreyeck/work/reading">Authoring the CTM Plan Page</a>, the entries of the <a page="CTM Plan Page WBS Dictionary" hyperbook="dreyeck/work/reading">CTM Plan Page WBS Dictionary</a> and the assignments and proposals of <a page="Implementation Assignments">Implementation Assignments</a> are written as a CTM document, read back with the topic-maps reader, and drawn with the native Topicmap renderer.</p>
 <p><a expr="(dreyeck/work/project:project-workspace)" view="Project">Open the HyperDoc Project Workspace</a>: the project and its Work Areas, the Work Items, the assignments, the proposals and the gaps, each a way into the Workspace. In the Workspace, the Point panel names where the Topic at Point is declared, links that declaration in its page source, and lists its Associations. Following an Association moves the Point; History keeps where it was.</p>
+<p>The proposed scope of Zettel 11359 is presented on <a page="Regular HyperDoc Catalog Scope Proposal">Regular HyperDoc Catalog Scope Proposal</a>: its Work Item, Deliverable, work packages, plan steps and preconditions, linked to where they are proposed. That page is not a source and declares nothing.</p>
 <p><a expr="(dreyeck/work/project:project-ctm-document)" view="CTM document">The project CTM document</a>: its octets, their SHA-256, what the topic-maps reader made of them, and the download of exactly those octets.</p>
 
 <h2>Authority</h2>
